<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Aberconwy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1277">1277</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conquest-of-wales-by-edward-i">Conquest of Wales by Edward I</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Aberconwy was the settlement imposed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-i-of-england">Edward I of England</a> on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/llywelyn-ap-gruffudd">Llywelyn ap Gruffudd</a> in November 1277, ending their first war. Llywelyn kept the title of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-of-wales">Prince of Wales</a> but lost the homage of most Welsh lords and was confined to Gwynedd west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-conwy">River Conwy</a>, and he agreed to a large indemnity, later remitted. Resentment of its terms contributed to the war of 1282–1283.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-aberconwy.jpg" alt="Treaty of Aberconwy" width="320" height="274" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AlexD · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gwynedd_after_the_Treaty_of_Aberconwy_1277.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
